<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Standard's Coleman to join J.P. Morgan.</title>
<headline>Standard's Coleman to join J.P. Morgan.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard Corporate and Merchant Bank's (SCMB) Colin Coleman would leave the bank to take up a post at J.P. Morgan in London as a vice president, the bank said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Coleman, currently director, public finance at SCMB, would leave the bank on July 31, it said.</p>
<p>SCMB managing director Jacko Maree paid tribute to Coleman for his role in setting up the 806 million rand South Africa Infrastructure Fund and other initiatives.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
